    <string name="legacy_adb_intro">LelloStore first tries the local ADB service on port 5555. This enables unattended installations without keeping Wireless Debugging switched on.</string>
    <string name="legacy_adb_step_one">1. Connect this device to a trusted computer over USB and authorize that computer if Android asks.</string>
    <string name="legacy_adb_step_two">2. With Android Platform Tools installed, run:</string>
    <string name="legacy_adb_command">adb tcpip 5555</string>
    <string name="legacy_adb_step_three">3. Return to LelloStore and tap “Test connection”. Android may ask once whether LelloStore may use ADB.</string>
    <string name="legacy_adb_security_warning">Security note: Android listens on all network interfaces. Use this only on a trusted private network. Most phones close port 5555 after reboot, so repeat provisioning when necessary.</string>
    <string name="adb_connection_not_tested">Tap to set up or test</string>
    <string name="adb_connection_testing">Testing connection…</string>
