    <string name="adb_connection_unavailable">Unavailable · %1$s</string>
    <string name="wireless_debugging_setup_intro">LelloStore uses Android’s encrypted Wireless Debugging connection to install updates without confirmation prompts. Pairing normally survives a reboot, even when Android switches Wireless Debugging off.</string>
    <string name="wireless_debugging_step_one">1. Connect this device to Wi‑Fi.</string>
    <string name="wireless_debugging_step_two">2. Open Developer settings with the button below and enable Wireless debugging.</string>
    <string name="wireless_debugging_step_three">3. Before requesting a code, put Android Settings and LelloStore side by side using split screen. Android may cancel pairing if Settings leaves the screen.</string>
    <string name="wireless_debugging_step_four">4. For first-time setup only, choose “Pair device with pairing code” in Settings. Enter that code below, then pair and test. If this device was paired before, simply re-enable Wireless Debugging and use “Test connection”.</string>
